                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَافِلَةٌ</span></b> 
                        : the pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَوَافِلُ</span>, is explained in the TA,
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حرز</span>, by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَوَائِدُ</span> [<i>Accessions,</i> or <i>additions</i>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<i>What accedes to,</i> or <i>exceeds, the original.</i> (T.)
<i>A voluntary gift, by way of alms,</i> or <i>as a good
work:</i> (T:) <i>a gift:</i> (K:) or <i>a gift</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنْ يَدٍ</span>:
(M:) <i>a deed beyond what is incumbent,</i> or
<i>obligatory.</i> (M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَافِلَةٌ</span>
                        <i>Supererogatory
prayer.</i> (S, Msb.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَطَوَّعَ</span>.

